.\nHand 20: Villain SB limped with 7d Kh. Hero BB checked (Ad 4s). Flop Td 9s 6h: villain bet 3 with K-high air (pure bluff), hero folded. Villain +2.\nHand 21: Villain BB held 8s 3c — hero SB folded 7s 6h preflop. No action from villain.\nHand 22: Villain SB limped. Hero BB (Td Th) checked preflop. Flop 3d 2h Tc: hero checked, villain bet 3, hero raised to 14, villain called. Turn Ad: hero bet 22, villain folded. Hero +16. No showdown.\nHand 23: Villain BB held Tc 2h — hero SB folded Ad 5s preflop. No action from villain.\nHand 24: Villain SB limped (hole unknown). Hero BB checked (5h 4c). Flop Td 8s 6h: hero checked, villain bet 3, hero raised to 14, villain FOLDED. Hero +5. No showdown.\nHand 25: Villain BB held 8h 7c — hero SB folded 7d Ks preflop. No action from villain.\nHand 26: Villain SB limped with Jc 3h. Hero BB checked (Kd 5h). Board 7d Qh Ah 7c 4h: all streets checked down. Showdown — villain Jc 3h (one pair 7s) lost to hero Kd 5h (one pair 7s, K kicker). Hero +2.\nHand 27: Villain BB held Td 8h — hero SB folded 8d 2d preflop. No action from villain.\nHand 28: Villain SB RAISED to 12 (larger than usual!) with Ac As. Hero BB folded 8s 9c. Hero -2.\nHand 29: Villain BB held Js 8h — hero SB folded 9c Jh preflop. No action from villain.\nHand 30: Villain SB FOLDED preflop. Hero BB (3h 5c) wins +1.\nHand 31: Hero SB folded Kd 9h preflop. Villain BB held Js 5s — no action from villain.\nHand 32: Villain SB limped with 6h Qc. Flop 6d 9d 2h: villain bet 3 with bottom pair (6s), hero folded Ah 3d. Villain +2.\nHand 33: Villain BB held 2c 8h — hero SB folded 4c Qh preflop. No action from villain.\nHand 34: Villain SB limped with 6d Jd. Hero BB checked (Kc 5s). Flop Qd 6c 4h: villain bet 3 with middle pair (6s), hero folded. Villain +2.\nHand 35: Villain BB held 6h 5s — hero SB folded 5h 2s preflop. No action from villain.\nHand 36: Villain SB limped with 8c Tc. Hero BB checked (Ad 6c). Flop 3c 9d 7s: villain bet 3 with OESD (T-8 on 7-9 board), hero folded. Villain +2.\nHand 37: Villain BB held Ts Kd — hero SB folded 8d Jd preflop. No action from villain.\nHand 38: Villain SB limped with 2s 8d. Hero BB checked (Kc As). Flop Kd 7d Ks: hero checked, villain bet 3 with pure air (no pair, no draw), hero FOLDED trip kings. Villain +2. Hero major exploit miss.\nHand 39: Villain BB held Kh 8d — hero SB folded 6c Kc preflop. No action from villain.\nHand 40: Villain SB limped with 6h Ts. Hero BB checked (Js Jd). Flop Kd 6d Jh: hero checked, villain bet 3 with middle pair (6s), hero FOLDED trip jacks. Villain +2. Hero major exploit miss (3rd monster folded to small flop bet: H22 was correct, H38 trips, H40 trips).\nHand 41: Villain BB held 2d 8c — hero SB folded 4h 7s preflop. No action from villain.\n\nSummary (41 hands):\n- Preflop SB: Limps 14/26 SB opportunities; RAISED 3/26 with strong hands; FOLDED 1/26 (H30). Raise to 8 = suited ace (H10, H14). Raise to 12 = pocket aces (H28). SIZING TELL: bigger raise = stronger hand.\n- Preflop BB: 3-bets strong hands (1/1, AJd). Otherwise passive.\n- Postflop flop (after SB limp, villain initiative): Bets VERY wide — top pair, middle pair, bottom pair, draws (OESD), AND pure air. 10 flop bets revealed: 5 pair+, 2 draw/semi-bluff, 3 pure bluff/weak.\n- *** CRITICAL EXPLOIT ***: NEVER fold to villain's small flop bet (3). Hero has now folded trip jacks (H40) and trip kings (H38) — losing massive value. Always raise or call strong hands.\n- Folds to hero flop raise after villain bet: 2/2 (H24 immediate fold; H22 called then folded turn). KEY EXPLOIT.\n- Postflop turn: Raises turn with strong made hand for value (H16: two pair). Turn raise = very strong.\n- Folds to turn bet after checking flop passively: 1/1 (H6).\n- Folds to flop bet after limp (no initiative): 1/1 (H12).",
