n +2.\nHand 37: Villain BB held Ts Kd — hero SB folded 8d Jd preflop. No action from villain.\nHand 38: Villain SB limped with 2s 8d. Hero BB checked (Kc As). Flop Kd 7d Ks: hero checked, villain bet 3 with pure air (no pair, no draw), hero FOLDED trip kings. Villain +2. Hero major exploit miss.\nHand 39: Villain BB held Kh 8d — hero SB folded 6c Kc preflop. No action from villain.\nHand 40: Villain SB limped with 6h Ts. Hero BB checked (Js Jd). Flop Kd 6d Jh: hero checked, villain bet 3 with middle pair (6s), hero FOLDED trip jacks. Villain +2. Hero major exploit miss.\nHand 41: Villain BB held 2d 8c — hero SB folded 4h 7s preflop. No action from villain.\nHand 42: Villain SB limped with 5c 6h. Hero BB checked (6c 8c). Flop Kh 5s 7c: villain bet 3 with bottom pair (5s) + gutshot, hero folded. Villain +2.\nHand 43: Villain BB held 9d Js — hero SB folded 2s 7c preflop. No action from villain.\nHand 44: Villain SB limped with 6s Qs. Hero BB checked (Js 4c). Flop 2s 5d 2d: villain bet 3 with Q-high air (pure bluff), hero folded. Villain +2.\nHand 45: Villain BB held 6c Qc — hero SB folded 9d 6h preflop. No action from villain.\nHand 46: Villain SB RAISED to 8 with 8h 8d (pocket eights). Hero BB folded 2c Tc. Hero -2.\nHand 47: Villain BB held Qs 5h — hero SB folded Ah 4d preflop. No action from villain.\nHand 48: Villain SB limped with 2d Jh. Hero BB checked (3c 4c). Flop Qs Qc Ts: villain bet 3 with J-high air (pure bluff), hero folded. Villain +2.\nHand 49: Villain BB held Qd 6d — hero SB folded 2s Kc preflop. No action from villain.\nHand 50: Villain SB limped with 8h Qd. Hero BB checked (9c Ac). Flop 3d 8s Ad: villain bet 3 with middle pair (8s), hero FOLDED top pair ace. Villain +2. Hero major exploit miss.\nHand 51: Hero SB folded 7c Td preflop. Villain BB held 9c Th — no action from villain.\nHand 52: Villain SB limped with 9d Ts. Hero BB checked (3c 3h). Flop 5d 3d 4c: villain bet 3 with flush draw + straight outs (semi-bluff), hero FOLDED SET OF THREES. Villain +2. Hero major exploit miss (5th such fold).\nHand 53: Villain BB held 9s 4c — hero SB folded 6c Qc preflop. No action from villain.\nHand 54: Villain SB limped with 3d 4c. Hero BB checked (7h 2s). Flop 9c 8s 6c: villain bet 3 with weak draw (3-4 gutshot/backdoor on 6-8-9 board), hero folded 72o (correct fold). Villain +2.\nHand 55: Villain BB held 3s 4d — hero SB folded Tc 2s preflop. No action from villain.\nHand 56: Villain SB limped with 7c 8c. Hero BB checked (7h 2h). Flop 3c 4d 6d: villain bet 3 with OESD (7-8 on 3-4-6), hero folded 72o (correct fold). Villain +2.\nHand 57: Villain BB held Tc 8d — hero SB folded 6d 3h preflop. No action from villain.\nHand 58: Villain SB limped with Kd 9c. Hero BB checked (3c Ah). Flop Tc 9s 3s: villain bet 3 with middle pair (9s), hero FOLDED bottom pair + top kicker (Ah). Villain +2. Hero folded a pair — missed call.\nHand 59: Villain BB held Kc 9c — hero SB folded Qh Tc preflop. No action from villain.\nHand 60: Villain SB RAISED to 8 with Qs Qc. Hero BB folded As 7c. Hero -2.\nHand 61: Villain BB held 5s 9d — hero SB folded 3c 5c preflop. No action from villain.\nHand 62: Villain SB limped with 8h 9c. Hero BB checked (4h 9h). Flop 3d Jc Ad: villain bet 3 with 9-high pure air (no pair, no draw), hero folded. Villain +2. Hero had air too — fold was reasonable.\nHand 63: Villain BB held 7c 8h — hero SB folded 8c 7d preflop. No action from villain.\n\nSummary (63 hands):\n- Preflop SB: Limps 23/48 SB opportunities; RAISED 5/48 (H10: A4s→8, H14: A8o→8, H28: AA→12, H46: 88→8, H60: QQ→8); FOLDED 1/48 (H30).\n- SIZING TELL: Raise to 8 = aces (suited/offsuit) OR pocket pairs (88, QQ confirmed). Raise to 12 = AA (1 sample).\n- Preflop BB: 3-bets strong hands (1/1, AJd). Otherwise passive.\n- Postflop flop (after SB limp, villain initiative): Bets VERY wide — top pair, middle pair, bottom pair, draws (OESD, flush draw, gutshot), AND pure air. 19 flop bets revealed: 7 pair, 5 draws/semi-bluff, 7 pure bluff/air.\n- *** CRITICAL EXPLOIT ***: NEVER fold to villain's small flop bet (3) with any pair or better. Hero has folded trip kings (H38), trip jacks (H40), top pair ace (H50), set of threes (H52), and bottom pair+A kicker (H58). Always raise or call any pair or better.\n- Folds to hero flop raise after villain bet: 2/2 (H24 immediate fold; H22 called then folded turn). KEY EXPLOIT.\n- Postflop turn: Raises turn with strong made hand for value (H16: two pair). Turn raise = very strong.\n- Folds to turn bet after checking flop passively: 1/1 (H6).\n- Folds to flop bet after limp (no initiative): 1/1 (H12).",
